{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat control-reader-brief.md controls/control-packet-2.json'","aggregated_output":"# Stage B: reading the control theses (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reader. Do not edit files, run model calls or start runs, and do not read any file other than this brief\nand the one packet you are given.\n\nEach item of your packet pairs a **ruler question** (a question written by hand for an earlier, frozen measurement, with its\nunit, due day and ladder of rungs) with a **judged question** the system wrote itself for a thesis it opened (its question, the\noutcome it looks at, due day, year and rungs). It also lists **reader B's decisive items**: the evidence an earlier reader, called\nreader B, cited for the frozen answer to the ruler question (each with its day, title, passage and meaning), and **the evidence\nshown to the judge**: every evidence entry the system's judge was shown for the judged question in any of its requests on or\nbefore 2026-07-14 (empty when there is none). You are not told either answer, and you do not judge which answer is right.\n\nFor each item, answer three questions.\n\n1. `same_question`: **yes** when the judged question asks what the ruler question asks: the same quantity measured the same way\n   (the same total, scope and unit: not a part of it, a ceiling on it, another quantity or another unit), or the same event,\n   for the same period. **no** otherwise. Wording may differ; a judged question that asks for more or less than the ruler's,\n   or for another period, is **no**.\n2. `same_due`: for an **event** (a yes-or-no question), **yes** only when the judged question's deadline is the ruler's\n   deadline. For a **figure**, **yes** when the two due days both mark the publication of the same period's figure (for\n   example, both the annual report of the same fiscal year, even if the two days differ); **no** otherwise.\n3. `items`: for **each** of reader B's decisive items, by its id, **shown** when its content is present in the evidence shown to\n   the judge (the same fact or figure, in any wording, from any source), **not_shown** when it is absent. Search the entries for\n   the figure or the fact; do not mark an item shown because a related item is.\n\nReturn one JSON object per item, one per line, in packet order, and nothing else (no prose, no code fence):\n`{\"control\": 3, \"same_question\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"same_due\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"items\": {\"i005\": \"shown\"|\"not_shown\", ...}, \"why\": \"one sentence naming what decides each no and each not_shown\"}`.\n\n## Third reader (only where the two readers differ)\n\nA third reader of each family is given this brief, the packet, and a list of the disputed points, each a control number and a\nfield (`same_question`, `same_due`, or `item <id>`), without the two readers' answers. For each point, answer that one question\nafresh by the rules above and return one JSON object per point, one per line, and nothing else:\n`{\"control\": 3, \"field\": \"item i005\", \"ruling\": \"yes\"|\"no\"|\"shown\"|\"not_shown\", \"why\": \"one sentence\"}` (`yes`/`no` for the two\nquestion fields, `shown`/`not_shown` for an item).\n[\n {\n  \"control\": 5,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Rubin Ultra generation, in Kyber NVL144 racks, by December 31, 2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has begun shipping Rubin Ultra systems by December 31, 2027.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not begun shipping Rubin Ultra systems by December 31, 2027.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v8\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by December 31, 2028?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Whether NVIDIA begins shipping its Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by the end of 2028.\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2028\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has begun shipping the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by 2028-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not begun shipping the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by 2028-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i100\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis (a research firm's report, not NVIDIA)\",\n     \"what\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack for Vera Rubin Ultra delayed; cause: PCB midplane manufacturability\",\n     \"how_much\": \"more than 12 months\",\n     \"period\": \"from 2027 to 2028\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i179\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop\",\n    \"passage\": \"The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"four-die Rubin Ultra cancelled; two-die version remains\",\n     \"how_much\": \"roughly half the real-world compute\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\",\n     \"status_note\": \"cancelled\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i181\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis, about NVIDIA's plan\",\n     \"what\": \"sell more Oberon-Rubin racks to cover the Kyber gap\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\",\n     \"status_note\": \"as claimed\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i101\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Our roadmap is intact\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"rejects the SemiAnalysis report; says its roadmap (Rubin Ultra / Kyber in 2027) is unchanged\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i197\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\",\n    \"passage\": \"An Nvidia representative responded with a short statement to Tom's Hardware : \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA representative\",\n     \"what\": \"denies the report: roadmap intact\",\n     \"condition\": \"unclear whether the original or an already updated roadmap is meant\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e77 [rumour; Investing.com, summarizing SemiAnalysis’s weekend report; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack architecture would be delayed to 2028 because of PCB midplane manufacturing challenges.\\n    Quote: Supply chain research firm SemiAnalysis claimed in a weekend report that Nvidia's highly anticipated Kyber NVL144 rack architecture will be delayed to 2028 due to manufacturing challenges with its PCB midplane.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e82, e87; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e78 [party_statement; NVIDIA spokesperson, in a statement emailed to Investing.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remained intact, rejecting reports of delays to its next-generation server architectures.\\n    Quote: An Nvidia spokesperson swiftly refuted such claims in a brief statement emailed to Investing.com, stating: \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\",\n   \"- e79 [rumour; Investing.com, summarizing SemiAnalysis’s weekend report; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis alleged that NVIDIA cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design after operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\\n    Quote: The research firm further alleged that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e84; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e81 [third_party_view; Investing.com, reporting analysts cited by Bloomberg; original source Analysts cited by Bloomberg ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Analysts cited by Bloomberg said reported technical setbacks could severely limit NVIDIA’s future hardware scale-up capacity and widen the competitive opportunity for AMD’s MI500X and Broadcom-backed custom TPUs.\\n    Quote: According to analysts cited by Bloomberg, these rumored technical setbacks could severely cap the scale-up capacity of Nvidia's future hardware. This perceived vulnerability may create a wider competitive window for alternative AI platforms, specifically AMD's MI500X and Broadcom-backed custom TPUs.\",\n   \"- e82 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s Kyber rack-scale server design has been delayed by more than a year, from 2027 to 2028.\\n    Quote: Research firm SemiAnalysis reported that Kyber, Nvidia’s next rack-scale server design, has been pushed back more than a year , from 2027 to 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e77; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e83 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source tikr.com (analyst) 2026-07-06; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] The article reported that Nvidia’s NVL576 system may be delayed or ship only in small volumes.\\n    Quote: A larger version, called NVL576, which links eight racks together via optical connections, is also likely to be delayed or to ship only in small volumes.\",\n   \"- e84 [rumour; tikr.com (analyst); original source Cloud customers ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] Cloud customers reportedly rejected Nvidia’s proposed design combining two current-generation racks, citing awkward design and high operating costs.\\n    Quote: Cloud customers reportedly rejected it because the design was awkward and the service was expensive to run.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e79; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e85 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said Nvidia currently lacks a proven way to scale Rubin Ultra, potentially giving AMD and Google an opening in high-end AI chips.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis says this leaves Nvidia without a proven way to scale up Rubin Ultra for now, which could give rivals like AMD and Google an opening at the high end of the AI chip market.\",\n   \"- e87 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c0432377817a1c00a1bbadf0 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 had hit printed-circuit-board construction setbacks, contributing to a reported delay of more than a year.\\n    Quote: Research firm SemiAnalysis said in an X post that Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 hit setbacks in the construction of printed circuit boards for the platform.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e77; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e88 [third_party_view; Shawn Oh, quoted by businesstimes.com.sg; original source Shawn Oh, head of Korea cash equities at NH Investment & Securities ; from gnews:c0432377817a1c00a1bbadf0 2026-07-06] Shawn Oh of NH Investment & Securities said the prospect of a Kyber NVL144 delay was raising uncertainty around Nvidia’s next-generation scale-out roadmap and creating a wider competitive window for alternative AI platforms.\\n    Quote: The prospect of a Kyber NVL144 delay together with other points in the post are “raising uncertainty around Nvidia’s next-generation scale-out roadmap and creating a wider competitive window for alternative AI platforms,” he added.\",\n   \"- e78 [party_statement; NVIDIA spokesperson, in a statement emailed to Investing.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remained intact, rejecting reports of delays to its next-generation server architectures.\\n    Quote: An Nvidia spokesperson swiftly refuted such claims in a brief statement emailed to Investing.com, stating: \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e98, e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e82 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s Kyber rack-scale server design has been delayed by more than a year, from 2027 to 2028.\\n    Quote: Research firm SemiAnalysis reported that Kyber, Nvidia’s next rack-scale server design, has been pushed back more than a year , from 2027 to 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e77, e97, e104; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e97 [third_party_view; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:b48593184704bbbe6eddbc03 2026-07-07] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia was at least a year behind on manufacturing its next line of server racks.\\n    Quote: a research report claiming the AI leader was at least a year behind on manufacturing of its next line of server racks\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e82; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e98 [party_statement; CNBC; original source Nvidia 2026-07-06; from gnews:b48593184704bbbe6eddbc03 2026-07-07] Nvidia disputed SemiAnalysis’s report that its next-generation Kyber server rack was running into delays.\\n    Quote: the company disputed a report by SemiAnalysis that its next-gen Kyber server rack was running into delays\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e78; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e104 [third_party_view; 247Wallst.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 launch had moved from 2027 to 2028.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis reported on July 5–6, 2026 that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack-scale AI system has been delayed, from its planned 2027 launch to 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e82; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e105 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com, quoting an NVIDIA spokesperson via Bloomberg; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remained intact, disputing the reported Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA publicly disputed the report on Monday, with a spokesperson telling Bloomberg its “roadmap is intact.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e78; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e87 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c0432377817a1c00a1bbadf0 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 had hit printed-circuit-board construction setbacks, contributing to a reported delay of more than a year.\\n    Quote: Research firm SemiAnalysis said in an X post that Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 hit setbacks in the construction of printed circuit boards for the platform.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e77, e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e116 [third_party_view; Futuriom, relaying SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack system had hit manufacturing setbacks.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s stock also suffered this week because research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks—a situation that could be further impetus for NVIDIA to deploy its new credit and revenue-sharing model, creating a continuing flow of demand for its products.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e87; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e105 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com, quoting an NVIDIA spokesperson via Bloomberg; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remained intact, disputing the reported Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA publicly disputed the report on Monday, with a spokesperson telling Bloomberg its “roadmap is intact.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e78, e128; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e128 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia denied reports that Kyber could be delayed until 2028, saying its roadmap remains on track; the article says Kyber is expected to launch in 2027.\\n    Quote: Recently, Nvidia faced reports that suggested its next-generation Kyber rack-scale AI infrastructure could be delayed until 2028. However, the company denied the speculation, maintaining that its roadmap remains on track. Designed for the Rubin Ultra platform, Kyber is expected to launch in 2027 as an integrated AI infrastructure system and a key component of Nvidia's long-term AI infrastructure s\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e105 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com, quoting an NVIDIA spokesperson via Bloomberg; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remained intact, disputing the reported Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA publicly disputed the report on Monday, with a spokesperson telling Bloomberg its “roadmap is intact.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e78, e128, e199; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e199 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1c3c0c58ed5ec3da43292f9b 2026-07-11] NVIDIA denied reports that its Kyber platform is being delayed; the item gives no date for the denial.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) has denied reports that the Kyber platform is being delayed.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e200 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer, quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Semi Analysis ; from gnews:1c3c0c58ed5ec3da43292f9b 2026-07-11] Jim Cramer said Semi Analysis believes NVIDIA products could all be late because one part of its business is late; no specific product or timing was given.\\n    Quote: You know Semi Analysis does pretty good work, saying that everything could be late for NVIDIA because one particular part of their business is late.\",\n   \"- e77 [rumour; Investing.com, summarizing SemiAnalysis’s weekend report; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack architecture would be delayed to 2028 because of PCB midplane manufacturing challenges.\\n    Quote: Supply chain research firm SemiAnalysis claimed in a weekend report that Nvidia's highly anticipated Kyber NVL144 rack architecture will be delayed to 2028 due to manufacturing challenges with its PCB midplane.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e82, e87, e232; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e105 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com, quoting an NVIDIA spokesperson via Bloomberg; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remained intact, disputing the reported Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA publicly disputed the report on Monday, with a spokesperson telling Bloomberg its “roadmap is intact.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e78, e128, e199, e233; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e232 [third_party_view; fool.com (Geoffrey Seiler); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack system could be delayed until 2028 because of manufacturing difficulties with a crucial circuit board.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis reported that its Kyber NVL144 next-gen AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 due to troubles with manufacturing a crucial circuit board.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e77; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e233 [party_statement; fool.com (Geoffrey Seiler); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remains intact despite questions about a possible Kyber NVL144 delay.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has come out and said its roadmap remains intact, although questions linger.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e234 [third_party_view; fool.com (Geoffrey Seiler); original source Geoffrey Seiler 2026-07-12; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] Geoffrey Seiler said a delay to NVIDIA’s Kyber rack system could give AMD and Alphabet an opportunity to gain share in the high-end AI market.\\n    Quote: A delay could help open the door for Advanced Micro Devices ( AMD +2.91% ) and Alphabet ( GOOGL -0.36% ) ( GOOG -0.55% ) to gain a foothold in the high end of the AI market.\",\n   \"- e235 [fact; fool.com (Geoffrey Seiler); original source AMD ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] Geoffrey Seiler said AMD’s recent acquisition of memory-optimization software platform Mext, alongside its chiplet designs, positions AMD to offer a high-end server solution for inference.\\n    Quote: AMD's chiplet designs, which can package more memory onto its chips, and its recent acquisition of memory optimization software platform Mext, position it well to offer a high-end server solution designed specifically for inference.\",\n   \"- e236 [third_party_view; fool.com (Geoffrey Seiler); original source Geoffrey Seiler 2026-07-12; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] Geoffrey Seiler said Alphabet’s next-generation TPUs will be optimized for both AI training and inference.\\n    Quote: with its next generation, it will have chips optimized for both training and inference.\",\n   \"- e233 [party_statement; fool.com (Geoffrey Seiler); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remains intact despite questions about a possible Kyber NVL144 delay.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has come out and said its roadmap remains intact, although questions linger.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105, e353; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e353 [party_statement; EBC, quoting an Nvidia spokesperson; original source Nvidia spokesperson ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] An Nvidia spokesperson said the company's roadmap was intact, responding to reports of possible delays to the Kyber NVL144 architecture.\\n    Quote: Although an Nvidia spokesperson quickly countered the reports, telling that the company's \\\"roadmap is intact,\\\" the seeds of doubt were already sown.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e233; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
